    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u26.d02.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "would/could/might have + V3",
        "ru": "would/could/might have + V3"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "In the result of a third conditional, \"would have\" = certain result, \"could have\" = would have been able to, \"might have\" = a possible result. All use \"have + past participle\".",
        "ru": "В результате третьего типа условия «would have» = точный результат, «could have» = смог бы, «might have» = возможный результат. Все с «have + причастие»."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "would have (certain)",
            "ru": "would have (точно)"
          },
          "formula": "would have + V3",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "I would have called you.",
              "ru": "Я бы тебе позвонил."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "third-conditional"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "could have (able to)",
            "ru": "could have (смог бы)"
          },
          "formula": "could have + V3",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "We could have won the game.",
              "ru": "Мы могли бы выиграть игру."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "third-conditional"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "might have (possible)",
            "ru": "might have (возможно)"
          },
          "formula": "might have + V3",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "You might have got hurt.",
              "ru": "Ты мог бы пораниться."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "third-conditional"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "All three use \"have + V3\": \"could have won\", not \"could have win\".",
          "ru": "Все три с «have + V3»: «could have won», а не «could have win»."
        },
        {
          "en": "Never write \"would of / could of\" — it is \"would have / could have\".",
          "ru": "Никогда не пиши «would of / could of» — это «would have / could have»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u26.d02.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "A lucky escape",
        "ru": "Счастливая случайность"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u26.d02.reading.b1",
          "en": "It could have been a disaster. If the driver hadn't stopped in time, someone might have been badly hurt. \"We were so lucky,\" said Ben. \"If I had crossed a second earlier, the car would have hit me.\"",
          "ru": "Это могло обернуться катастрофой. Если бы водитель не остановился вовремя, кто-то мог бы серьёзно пострадать. «Нам так повезло, — сказал Бен. — Если бы я перешёл секундой раньше, машина бы меня сбила».",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u26.d02.reading.b1.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u26.d02.reading.b2",
          "en": "\"You should have looked both ways,\" his friend said. \"I know. It could have been much worse. But if the driver hadn't been paying attention, he couldn't have stopped so fast.\" They both agreed it had been a lucky escape.",
          "ru": "«Надо было смотреть в обе стороны», — сказал друг. «Знаю. Могло быть гораздо хуже. Но если бы водитель не был внимателен, он бы не смог так быстро затормозить». Оба согласились, что легко отделались.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u26.d02.reading.b2.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "word": "disaster",
          "ru": "катастрофа",
          "ipa": "/dɪˈzɑːstər/"
        },
